WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.036
- I wanted to be really successful,

00:00:02.036 --> 00:00:03.703
but not to just, like, get shoes;

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:06.656
I knew I wanted to make money

00:00:06.656 --> 00:00:08.400
because I wanted to make a difference.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.163
Listen to your gut and your heart,

00:00:10.163 --> 00:00:12.371
because, no matter what
any expert tells you,

00:00:12.371 --> 00:00:16.053
your wisdom inside needs to be paramount.

00:00:16.053 --> 00:00:18.432
When I was bartending,
I was fully bartending.

00:00:18.432 --> 00:00:19.861
Like, I wasn't talking to myself about:

00:00:19.861 --> 00:00:21.464
"Oh, my God, I should be
dancing right now," or,

00:00:21.464 --> 00:00:22.884
"I should be working on
my coaching practice."

00:00:22.884 --> 00:00:25.092
While I was growing my
personal coaching practice,

00:00:25.092 --> 00:00:27.653
I kept feeling conflicted because

00:00:27.653 --> 00:00:30.126
I didn't want to just be one thing.

00:00:30.126 --> 00:00:32.994
Are you guys here because
you want to be mediocre?

00:00:32.994 --> 00:00:34.489
- [Audience] No.

00:00:34.489 --> 00:00:36.870
- Mediocre sucks, does it not?

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.533
Don't get taken over by the
world's definition of success.

00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:43.478
It's like, everything that I've learned

00:00:43.478 --> 00:00:44.987
and I've been able to do in my business,

00:00:44.987 --> 00:00:46.464
we never know what's going to work.

00:00:46.464 --> 00:00:48.760
You should just engage an experience

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.441
and actually get your
foot in the industry.

00:00:50.441 --> 00:00:52.930
That can inform whether or
not you should move ahead.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:55.716
I have been this way,
meaning goofy, silly,

00:00:55.716 --> 00:00:58.519
since I was very, very little.

00:00:58.519 --> 00:00:59.566
You walk around your day, and you're like,

00:00:59.566 --> 00:01:01.002
"Wow, I have so many things
to do," and I'm like,

00:01:01.002 --> 00:01:04.065
"Wait a minute. This is
all awesome stuff to do."

00:01:04.065 --> 00:01:06.717
- She's an American life
coach, motivational speaker,

00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:08.514
author, and YouTuber.

00:01:08.514 --> 00:01:10.881
She's the owner and creator
of Marie Forleo International,

00:01:10.881 --> 00:01:13.361
B-School, and MarieTV.

00:01:13.361 --> 00:01:15.040
Forbes.com listed her website

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.823
as one of the top 100
websites for entrepreneurs.

00:01:17.823 --> 00:01:19.026
She's Marie Forleo,

00:01:19.026 --> 00:01:22.609
and here are her top
ten rules for success.

00:01:24.239 --> 00:01:27.182
- You know, my first gig out
of college was on Wall Street,

00:01:27.182 --> 00:01:29.351
on the New York Stock Exchange, and-

00:01:29.351 --> 00:01:30.567
- [Interviewer] This is pre-?

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:31.620
- This is pre-everything.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.261
This is like, just out of
college, twenty-one years old,

00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:36.890
and I knew one of my drives:

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:38.726
I wanted to be really successful,

00:01:38.726 --> 00:01:40.396
but not to just, like, get shoes.

00:01:40.396 --> 00:01:43.273
I knew I wanted to make money

00:01:43.273 --> 00:01:45.135
because I wanted to make a difference.

00:01:45.135 --> 00:01:47.194
I wanted to be able to
take care of my family.

00:01:47.194 --> 00:01:49.282
I wanted to be able to contribute

00:01:49.282 --> 00:01:51.206
to causes that I believe in,

00:01:51.206 --> 00:01:53.057
and so I knew, in order to do that,

00:01:53.057 --> 00:01:54.653
in my own mind, I was like:

00:01:54.653 --> 00:01:55.963
"Well, I want to make a lot of money

00:01:55.963 --> 00:01:57.524
and make this stuff happen."

00:01:57.524 --> 00:01:59.030
But, when I was on Wall Street,

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:00.786
even though so many
people that I worked with-

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:04.538
multi-multi-millionaires, I
mean, the money was ridiculous-

00:02:04.538 --> 00:02:06.505
while they were financially rich,

00:02:06.505 --> 00:02:08.530
they were spiritually bankrupt.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:11.813
And I felt, like, there was a part of me

00:02:11.813 --> 00:02:13.598
that was dying inside, and I said,

00:02:13.598 --> 00:02:16.294
"This is not my path. I
don't know what my path is,

00:02:16.294 --> 00:02:19.102
but I need to leave this
because I feel sick."

00:02:19.102 --> 00:02:21.986
And so, I think many
people feel like that.

00:02:21.986 --> 00:02:24.017
You can find yourself a
job, and job, and job,

00:02:24.017 --> 00:02:25.550
and you want to do a really-

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.029
you want to do great work in the world,

00:02:27.029 --> 00:02:28.288
you're giving it your best,

00:02:28.288 --> 00:02:31.393
but some little voice inside
is saying "This isn't me."

00:02:31.393 --> 00:02:32.226
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:02:32.226 --> 00:02:33.059
- "This isn't me."

00:02:33.059 --> 00:02:34.201
And I kept having that voice

00:02:34.201 --> 00:02:37.095
until finally I left the corporate world

00:02:37.095 --> 00:02:38.926
and started my own business.

00:02:38.926 --> 00:02:41.262
- Listen to your gut, and your heart,

00:02:41.262 --> 00:02:43.438
because, no matter what
any expert tells you,

00:02:43.438 --> 00:02:46.821
your wisdom inside needs to be paramount.

00:02:46.821 --> 00:02:49.115
It needs to always drive
all of your decisions.

00:02:49.115 --> 00:02:50.862
Even, you know, when I
was first starting out,

00:02:50.862 --> 00:02:52.153
I would pay attention to people

00:02:52.153 --> 00:02:53.757
that absolutely knew what they were doing.

00:02:53.757 --> 00:02:55.701
They were completely
ethical, they were smart,

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.077
they were good teachers as well.

00:02:57.077 --> 00:02:59.590
Sometimes, their advice just
didn't sit right with me,

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:03.674
and if I wasn't as secure
in my own inner voice,

00:03:03.674 --> 00:03:05.449
I might have gone down paths

00:03:05.449 --> 00:03:07.253
that wouldn't have been that great.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.645
So, I think it's wonderful
to get an education,

00:03:09.645 --> 00:03:11.427
it's wonderful to take in experiences,

00:03:11.427 --> 00:03:14.349
but never, ever, ever
listen to anything other

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:16.866
than what is that true voice within you,

00:03:16.866 --> 00:03:18.004
and that takes practice.

00:03:18.004 --> 00:03:20.422
- When I was bartending,
I was fully bartending.

00:03:20.422 --> 00:03:21.912
Like, I wasn't talking to myself about:

00:03:21.912 --> 00:03:23.625
"Oh, my God, I should be
dancing right now," or,

00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:24.964
"I should be working on
my coaching practice."

00:03:24.964 --> 00:03:27.054
I was just really into bartending,

00:03:27.054 --> 00:03:29.022
and, when I was dancing,
I was like, you know,

00:03:29.022 --> 00:03:32.312
being the best hip-hop
teacher/dancer I could possibly be.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:34.436
When I was being a coach,
same kind of thing.

00:03:34.436 --> 00:03:37.959
And I think that practice
of being fully engaged,

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:39.307
in the thing that you're doing,

00:03:39.307 --> 00:03:40.585
conserves a ton of energy,

00:03:40.585 --> 00:03:42.160
and that's what most people don't do.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.267
- Part of what was also
challenging for me,

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.446
when I was starting off as a coach,

00:03:46.446 --> 00:03:49.097
was recognizing the truth:

00:03:49.097 --> 00:03:51.192
that I didn't just want to be a coach.

00:03:51.192 --> 00:03:54.270
I loved writing, I loved hip-hop,

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:57.154
I loved dance, I loved fitness.

00:03:57.154 --> 00:03:59.405
There were all these different things

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:00.772
that I was passionate about;

00:04:00.772 --> 00:04:03.321
and, while I was growing my
personal coaching practice,

00:04:03.321 --> 00:04:06.239
I kept feeling conflicted
because I didn't want

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:08.190
to just be one thing.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:09.580
Has anyone ever felt that way?

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:10.413
- [Interviewer laughs.]

00:04:10.413 --> 00:04:13.662
- Yeah. So, I would listen to the voices

00:04:13.662 --> 00:04:16.144
in my head which were like-
and, basically, the voices

00:04:16.144 --> 00:04:18.580
in my head were so trained
by traditional wisdom

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.189
and traditional thoughts about:

00:04:20.189 --> 00:04:22.754
"You have to pick a niche.
You have to narrow down.

00:04:22.754 --> 00:04:24.401
You have to choose one
thing and be good for it,

00:04:24.401 --> 00:04:27.965
be really good at it, and
that's how you'll be known."

00:04:27.965 --> 00:04:31.752
And, when I realized that
that voice wasn't the voice

00:04:31.752 --> 00:04:34.096
that I should listen to,
that there was this truth:

00:04:34.096 --> 00:04:36.084
that I was this multi-passionate person,

00:04:36.084 --> 00:04:37.818
and that living in the present moment,

00:04:37.818 --> 00:04:39.129
which Eckhart teaches,

00:04:39.129 --> 00:04:41.980
was all about really listening

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:45.556
to your own inner guidance
and being in the here and now,

00:04:45.556 --> 00:04:47.716
and not stressing so much up here.

00:04:47.716 --> 00:04:49.736
That really opened the door for me to say,

00:04:49.736 --> 00:04:51.025
"You know what? Screw it.

00:04:51.025 --> 00:04:52.927
I'm going to go take dance classes.

00:04:52.927 --> 00:04:54.497
I'm going to go learn about this.

00:04:54.497 --> 00:04:56.048
I'm going to do all
these different things."

00:04:56.048 --> 00:04:59.293
And that training, to be in the moment,

00:04:59.293 --> 00:05:00.697
and to listen to my own inner guidance,

00:05:00.697 --> 00:05:04.021
allowed me to disconnect from
all the B.S. voices in my head

00:05:04.021 --> 00:05:06.326
that were torturing me.

00:05:06.326 --> 00:05:07.201
Torturing me.

00:05:07.201 --> 00:05:09.013
- How would you behave if you
were the best in the world

00:05:09.013 --> 00:05:10.256
at what you do?

00:05:10.256 --> 00:05:14.271
How would that change what time
you wake up in the morning?

00:05:14.271 --> 00:05:18.812
How would that change the
food you put in your body?

00:05:18.812 --> 00:05:22.690
How would that change the
people you hang out with?

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.384
How you spend your time
throughout the day?

00:05:26.384 --> 00:05:28.384
What websites you visit?

00:05:29.443 --> 00:05:32.079
Whether or not you work from a schedule?

00:05:32.079 --> 00:05:33.721
If you were world class,

00:05:33.721 --> 00:05:35.309
and the best in the world at what you do,

00:05:35.309 --> 00:05:37.892
how would your behavior change?

00:05:38.898 --> 00:05:40.377
It's a really interesting question

00:05:40.377 --> 00:05:42.591
that I started asking
myself a few years ago,

00:05:42.591 --> 00:05:44.790
and, I will tell you, it
has changed everything.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:46.340
It's one of those singular questions;

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.937
whether you put it on your screensaver,

00:05:48.937 --> 00:05:51.598
you have a little reminder
on your cell phone,

00:05:51.598 --> 00:05:53.827
you have it on the top of a notebook;

00:05:53.827 --> 00:05:56.324
I guarantee you, if you
start looking at your world

00:05:56.324 --> 00:06:01.194
through this lens, it's
going to shift everything.

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:02.328
Now, let me ask you this,

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:03.899
just to back this up a little bit more:

00:06:03.899 --> 00:06:07.609
are you guys here because
you want to be mediocre?

00:06:07.609 --> 00:06:08.442
- [Audience] No.

00:06:08.442 --> 00:06:10.631
- Mediocre sucks, does it not?

00:06:10.631 --> 00:06:12.011
- [Audience] Yes!

00:06:12.011 --> 00:06:13.667
- We want to be world-class.

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.449
We want to be the best,
and let me ask you this:

00:06:15.449 --> 00:06:19.616
who's in charge of you
being the best in the world?

00:06:20.522 --> 00:06:23.046
Yes? Can I hear an "I am?"

00:06:23.046 --> 00:06:24.147
- [Audience] I am.

00:06:24.147 --> 00:06:25.363
- A little louder?

00:06:25.363 --> 00:06:26.196
- [Audience] I AM.

00:06:26.196 --> 00:06:27.029
- One more?

00:06:27.029 --> 00:06:27.862
- [Audience] I AM!

00:06:27.862 --> 00:06:30.414
- Amen, and it's not even
a Sunday. Okay, good.

00:06:30.414 --> 00:06:32.890
- If you had to give someone
who's recently graduating

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.158
from our program a piece of advice,

00:06:35.158 --> 00:06:36.288
what would you say?

00:06:36.288 --> 00:06:40.455
- I would say to learn and to
execute on your unique vision.

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.427
Define success for yourself.

00:06:43.427 --> 00:06:45.199
Figure out what that means to you.

00:06:45.199 --> 00:06:50.054
Don't get taken over by the
world's definition of success,

00:06:50.054 --> 00:06:52.023
or your family's, or what
your friends are doing,

00:06:52.023 --> 00:06:54.875
or what anyone says that equals success.

00:06:54.875 --> 00:06:56.711
Once you can get clear on that vision,

00:06:56.711 --> 00:06:59.973
then you need to create a plan
to make that come to life,

00:06:59.973 --> 00:07:01.442
and to prioritize.

00:07:01.442 --> 00:07:04.424
I think one of the biggest
tragedies of our time is:

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:07.053
I hear so many people
from every walk of life,

00:07:07.053 --> 00:07:08.416
health coaches, all over,

00:07:08.416 --> 00:07:11.428
feeling so overwhelmed, and overworked,

00:07:11.428 --> 00:07:13.731
and there's so much that they can do,

00:07:13.731 --> 00:07:15.076
that they feel paralyzed.

00:07:15.076 --> 00:07:16.352
"Well, I don't know what to do first,"

00:07:16.352 --> 00:07:18.426
"How do I make all of this happen,"

00:07:18.426 --> 00:07:19.720
and I think that we all need

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:22.561
to take a few steps back
and start to get clear

00:07:22.561 --> 00:07:24.110
on our own vision for success,

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.865
and then actually prioritize
making that come to life,

00:07:26.865 --> 00:07:29.802
because then it gives you such
clarity, and such freedom;

00:07:29.802 --> 00:07:32.438
and all of that static
and the overwhelm starts

00:07:32.438 --> 00:07:33.271
to fall away.

00:07:33.271 --> 00:07:35.144
- What if I actually follow my heart,

00:07:35.144 --> 00:07:36.784
and I don't make a living at it?

00:07:36.784 --> 00:07:40.875
All my friends say, "You
suck. See, I told you so?"

00:07:40.875 --> 00:07:42.623
Eckhart actually talked about
when, he was moving once,

00:07:42.623 --> 00:07:45.538
his parents said, "Really?
You're going to do this again?"

00:07:45.538 --> 00:07:47.238
Like, they'd seen him
as a failure for years,

00:07:47.238 --> 00:07:49.875
and then- anyways. There's
that, always that voice,

00:07:49.875 --> 00:07:51.462
that's like, "Yeah, yeah, yeah,"

00:07:51.462 --> 00:07:52.939
but you might just really fail.

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:55.872
- Yeah, and, you know, I
think all of us have that,

00:07:55.872 --> 00:07:59.120
and there's perhaps some
of them, like a myth,

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.331
that many of us can think,

00:08:00.331 --> 00:08:01.913
especially when we're first starting out,

00:08:01.913 --> 00:08:04.819
that successful people don't
have the voice anymore.

00:08:04.819 --> 00:08:06.474
That's total crap.

00:08:06.474 --> 00:08:08.921
Anyone that you've ever seen,
anyone that I've encountered,

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:10.390
and I've had the opportunity to interview

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:11.820
a lot of people and talk to them;

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.709
no matter how successful,
how accomplished,

00:08:14.709 --> 00:08:17.999
how well-known, they still have
those voices of self-doubt.

00:08:17.999 --> 00:08:19.299
They still get afraid.

00:08:19.299 --> 00:08:20.238
They still question:

00:08:20.238 --> 00:08:21.507
"Am I going in the right direction?

00:08:21.507 --> 00:08:22.795
What's next for me?"

00:08:22.795 --> 00:08:24.535
And, I think, the more
that we can recognize that

00:08:24.535 --> 00:08:28.481
that voice of, basically,
"You suck," is universal,

00:08:28.481 --> 00:08:32.296
and we can disengage from
that and actually engage

00:08:32.296 --> 00:08:34.688
with what we want in our lives,

00:08:34.688 --> 00:08:35.860
the happier we're going to be.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:38.642
And, this is the other
thing: none of us know.

00:08:38.642 --> 00:08:40.594
It's like, everything that I've learned

00:08:40.594 --> 00:08:41.960
and I've been able to do in my business,

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.764
we never know what's going to work.

00:08:43.764 --> 00:08:46.843
We treat every single
thing as an experiment.

00:08:46.843 --> 00:08:48.506
That's the only way that you learn.

00:08:48.506 --> 00:08:50.602
I think 99% of what each of us

00:08:50.602 --> 00:08:52.314
need to do to learn and grow,

00:08:52.314 --> 00:08:53.765
not only as businesspeople,

00:08:53.765 --> 00:08:56.486
but also as human beings,
if we're going to grow,

00:08:56.486 --> 00:08:58.637
it means that we've
never done that before.

00:08:58.637 --> 00:09:00.338
It's going to be uncomfortable.

00:09:00.338 --> 00:09:03.686
And, to be okay in that
uncertainty and that discomfort,

00:09:03.686 --> 00:09:05.419
is where the juice of life lives.

00:09:05.419 --> 00:09:09.024
- I really went into
pursuing different passions

00:09:09.024 --> 00:09:10.497
with eyes wide open; meaning:

00:09:10.497 --> 00:09:13.725
knowing, because my focus was split,

00:09:13.725 --> 00:09:16.527
I probably wouldn't be getting
very far in any of them;

00:09:16.527 --> 00:09:18.680
but I made a conscious
choice that I just wanted

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.836
to experience them.

00:09:20.836 --> 00:09:23.156
I wanted to understand
them from the inside out.

00:09:23.156 --> 00:09:25.864
I spent so much time thinking, in my mind,

00:09:25.864 --> 00:09:27.547
"Is this the right choice for me?

00:09:27.547 --> 00:09:28.968
Is this the right career for me?

00:09:28.968 --> 00:09:30.868
Should I try to build a
business around this?",

00:09:30.868 --> 00:09:33.385
and I said, "That's such a
dumb way to go around it."

00:09:33.385 --> 00:09:36.089
Like, you should just
engage and experience

00:09:36.089 --> 00:09:37.798
and actually get your
foot in the industry.

00:09:37.798 --> 00:09:40.585
That can inform whether or
not you should move ahead.

00:09:40.585 --> 00:09:43.162
- What about someone who's
stuck, or struggling?

00:09:43.162 --> 00:09:44.216
What would you tell them?

00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:46.995
- Stuck or struggling is typically someone

00:09:46.995 --> 00:09:49.177
who is more engaged in their thoughts

00:09:49.177 --> 00:09:50.652
than actually taking action.

00:09:50.652 --> 00:09:54.206
So, it's a really
interesting, subtle shift;

00:09:54.206 --> 00:09:55.966
but, if you catch
yourself complaining like,

00:09:55.966 --> 00:09:57.702
"Oh, I'm so stuck, and-"

00:09:57.702 --> 00:09:58.583
Stop.

00:09:58.583 --> 00:10:01.941
Write an e-mail, make a call, take a step,

00:10:01.941 --> 00:10:03.924
and the more you actually do that

00:10:03.924 --> 00:10:05.809
and catch yourself, we actually-

00:10:05.809 --> 00:10:10.270
Sorry, this is me, A.D.D., my
toes are exactly that color.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:11.103
- Awesome.
- Yes.

00:10:11.103 --> 00:10:12.705
- I love it.

00:10:12.705 --> 00:10:13.538
- But it is.

00:10:13.538 --> 00:10:16.532
It's really a practice of
checking in with yourself.

00:10:16.532 --> 00:10:18.206
You got to check yourself
before you wreck yourself.

00:10:18.206 --> 00:10:19.620
Like, stop complaining,

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:20.890
stop talking to yourself in your head,

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.245
and do something.

00:10:22.245 --> 00:10:26.166
I have been this way,
meaning goofy, silly,

00:10:26.166 --> 00:10:28.175
since I was very, very little.

00:10:28.175 --> 00:10:30.684
And, when I first started
my coaching practice

00:10:30.684 --> 00:10:31.977
when I was twenty-three,

00:10:31.977 --> 00:10:33.808
I tried to be what I thought

00:10:33.808 --> 00:10:35.825
in my mind was a "businesswoman".

00:10:35.825 --> 00:10:38.393
I had this idea of, like, a power suit,

00:10:38.393 --> 00:10:40.158
and some big old shoulder pads,

00:10:40.158 --> 00:10:41.747
and I would speak in a certain way,

00:10:41.747 --> 00:10:46.202
and I remember trying to do
that, and I felt horrible.

00:10:46.202 --> 00:10:47.405
Like, I felt so stunted.

00:10:47.405 --> 00:10:48.797
It was like I had writer's block.

00:10:48.797 --> 00:10:49.883
I had speaker's block.

00:10:49.883 --> 00:10:53.119
I just felt like I was
in somebody else's skin,

00:10:53.119 --> 00:10:55.524
and it was so painful for
me that I was just like,

00:10:55.524 --> 00:10:57.823
"I can't do this, but I
really want to do this thing.

00:10:57.823 --> 00:11:01.421
I'm going to let go of my idea
of who I think I should be,

00:11:01.421 --> 00:11:03.397
and talk about the fact I'm from Jersey,

00:11:03.397 --> 00:11:06.211
I don't use proper language all the time,

00:11:06.211 --> 00:11:08.430
I have kind of a weird sense of humor,

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.846
I love zombies, Smurfs,
all kinds of things,

00:11:10.846 --> 00:11:14.289
and what would happen if I
actually just expressed that?"

00:11:14.289 --> 00:11:16.330
And something funny
actually did happen, is:

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:19.694
not only did I find myself
to be more creative,

00:11:19.694 --> 00:11:21.430
I found myself more fulfilled,

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:24.044
and people actually
connected with me more.

00:11:24.044 --> 00:11:26.636
I didn't feel like I had to
push myself out into the world;

00:11:26.636 --> 00:11:29.768
it was more like things
started to come to me.

00:11:29.768 --> 00:11:31.658
And I didn't feel like there
was so much of a separation

00:11:31.658 --> 00:11:35.568
between my "work day"
and the rest of my life,

00:11:35.568 --> 00:11:36.803
which felt great.

00:11:36.803 --> 00:11:39.682
For me, a good life is a couple of things.

00:11:39.682 --> 00:11:43.055
One, being fully present in each moment,

00:11:43.055 --> 00:11:45.787
because I find that, when
I am fully present, like,

00:11:45.787 --> 00:11:48.206
you know, you and I having
this great conversation now,

00:11:48.206 --> 00:11:50.809
or if I'm with Josh and
we're just hanging out.

00:11:50.809 --> 00:11:52.759
It does not matter what we're doing,

00:11:52.759 --> 00:11:53.926
but I feel so-

00:11:55.118 --> 00:11:56.951
peaceful, and content,

00:11:57.997 --> 00:12:00.042
and like all is well in the world.

00:12:00.042 --> 00:12:04.519
Even if there's challenges,
I feel a sense of peace,

00:12:04.519 --> 00:12:06.040
and that's one component of it;

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:07.408
and, I think the other component, for me,

00:12:07.408 --> 00:12:10.060
of living a good life,
is having good friends

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:11.627
and having a lot of fun.

00:12:11.627 --> 00:12:12.880
I think any time that I slip

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.719
into taking things too seriously;

00:12:15.719 --> 00:12:17.344
like, you walk around in
your day, and you're like,

00:12:17.344 --> 00:12:18.684
"Wow, I have so many things to do,"

00:12:18.684 --> 00:12:19.672
and I'm like, "Wait a minute.

00:12:19.672 --> 00:12:21.572
This is all awesome stuff to do,

00:12:21.572 --> 00:12:23.099
and I set my life up this way.

00:12:23.099 --> 00:12:24.505
I'd better not take it so seriously,

00:12:24.505 --> 00:12:27.071
and have a little fun, and
put on some music and dance."

00:12:27.071 --> 00:12:31.018
When that kind of thread of
celebration and irreverence

00:12:31.018 --> 00:12:33.255
and not taking things too seriously-

00:12:33.255 --> 00:12:37.255
That's what living a good
life feels like to me.

00:12:38.766 --> 00:12:40.170
- Thank you guys so much for watching!

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:42.686
I made this video because
Ewelina asked me to;

00:12:42.686 --> 00:12:44.150
so, if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:46.078
that you want me to profile next,

00:12:46.078 --> 00:12:47.336
leave it in the comments below,

00:12:47.336 --> 00:12:48.557
and I'll join the discussion.

00:12:48.557 --> 00:12:50.798
I'd also love to know which
of Marie's top ten rules

00:12:50.798 --> 00:12:53.006
meant the most to you, and
had the biggest impact.

00:12:53.006 --> 00:12:55.312
Leave it in the comments and
I'll join the discussion.

00:12:55.312 --> 00:12:56.527
And, one last thing:

00:12:56.527 --> 00:12:58.881
my personal goal is to hit
one million subscribers

00:12:58.881 --> 00:13:01.162
on this channel, so anything
that you can think of

00:13:01.162 --> 00:13:04.073
to share the video, tweet
it, add the playlist,

00:13:04.073 --> 00:13:05.679
tell your friends about it,

00:13:05.679 --> 00:13:07.932
I'd really, really, really,
really appreciate it.

00:13:07.932 --> 00:13:09.000
Thank you guys so much!

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:12.583
Continue to believe,
and I'll see you soon.

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:19.073
- The fact that,

00:13:20.457 --> 00:13:23.190
when you're good at
whatever you're good at;

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:26.160
so, for me, I was so
passionate about spirituality

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.305
and personal development,

00:13:27.305 --> 00:13:31.139
and all of the tools that
come in that toolbox;

00:13:31.139 --> 00:13:35.425
but recognizing you also have
to know how to run a business.

00:13:35.425 --> 00:13:38.017
Being good at something
isn't the same thing as

00:13:38.017 --> 00:13:40.545
being able to run a
business doing that thing.

00:13:40.545 --> 00:13:42.979
And I recognized very
quickly that I needed

00:13:42.979 --> 00:13:44.977
to understand how to market,

00:13:44.977 --> 00:13:47.143
and I wanted to use these new online tools

00:13:47.143 --> 00:13:49.400
specifically because I was so embarrassed

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:51.610
about my age because I was so young,

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:53.391
that I wanted to use the
internet, which I did,

00:13:53.391 --> 00:13:54.641
to mask my age.

00:13:55.527 --> 00:13:57.895
And I never lied, but I got headshots done

00:13:57.895 --> 00:13:59.807
that made me look much older than I was,

00:13:59.807 --> 00:14:01.330
and I put up a website,

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:04.571
and all of my clients came
to me through the internet;

00:14:04.571 --> 00:14:07.756
and, if they didn't ask how
old I was, I didn't tell them.

00:14:07.756 --> 00:14:09.386
I just did the best work I could.

00:14:09.386 --> 00:14:11.103
But that key lesson about:

00:14:11.103 --> 00:14:14.245
even if you love something,
and even if it's your passion,

00:14:14.245 --> 00:14:18.735
you have to also get passionate
about entrepreneurship.

00:14:18.735 --> 00:14:19.669
- [Interviewer] If you want
to make a living at it.

00:14:19.669 --> 00:14:22.757
- If you want to make a living
at it as a solo entrepreneur,

00:14:22.757 --> 00:14:24.252
as a business owner.

00:14:24.252 --> 00:14:26.991
- Nothing will kill your business faster

00:14:26.991 --> 00:14:30.074
than being lost in a crowd of sameys.

00:14:31.219 --> 00:14:34.162
How many people here ever
feel like you look around,

00:14:34.162 --> 00:14:37.658
and it's like: "Everybody's
doing the same shit!"

00:14:37.658 --> 00:14:40.342
Right? Do you feel like that?

00:14:40.342 --> 00:14:42.271
Everybody starts copying each other,

00:14:42.271 --> 00:14:43.508
and it all starts to look the same,

00:14:43.508 --> 00:14:45.248
and it all starts to sound the same,

00:14:45.248 --> 00:14:46.995
so positioning is all about

00:14:46.995 --> 00:14:50.316
positioning yourself
to be vastly different.

00:14:50.316 --> 00:14:51.915
This is probably one of my favorite parts

00:14:51.915 --> 00:14:52.869
of this presentation.

00:14:52.869 --> 00:14:55.575
I'm going to teach you
something that is so damn good.

00:14:55.575 --> 00:14:58.344
I promise, if you do this
for your whole business

00:14:58.344 --> 00:15:00.505
and every product or service you have,

00:15:00.505 --> 00:15:03.303
you'll be able to articulate
very, very clearly

00:15:03.303 --> 00:15:04.706
exactly how you are different;

00:15:04.706 --> 00:15:06.938
and, more importantly
than articulating it,

00:15:06.938 --> 00:15:09.342
it's going to be a
living, breathing essence

00:15:09.342 --> 00:15:12.637
of how you stand apart
from everybody else.

00:15:12.637 --> 00:15:14.304
- I feel like I love

00:15:16.403 --> 00:15:20.444
the process of learning and
discovering new things so much,

00:15:20.444 --> 00:15:22.556
and I love seeing other people win.

00:15:22.556 --> 00:15:25.731
So, like, learning these
new ideas and new skills

00:15:25.731 --> 00:15:27.514
that I've never been exposed to before,

00:15:27.514 --> 00:15:30.225
and then being able to
teach them to other people

00:15:30.225 --> 00:15:32.923
and watch the ah-hah
moments or the breakthroughs

00:15:32.923 --> 00:15:35.810
or the progress happen for them.

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:37.475
I love seeing other people win.

00:15:37.475 --> 00:15:39.161
So that's what kept driving me,

00:15:39.161 --> 00:15:39.994
and I was like:

00:15:39.994 --> 00:15:40.905
"Wow, if I could do this with five people,

00:15:40.905 --> 00:15:42.304
I could do this with, like, twenty people,

00:15:42.304 --> 00:15:44.372
or a hundred people,
or a thousand people,"

00:15:44.372 --> 00:15:46.279
and it was really exciting.

